! jb_ax5b "I-Box 5", routine 1262 ("TEST EX AND EXIC"), TEST 3A --
! "-TEST 3A, PSEUDO IC LESS THAN 15." -- entry label 162100, PDF
! pp.107-108, octal 024136.00-024151.00.  23 half-words.
!
! CITED BY PDF PAGE, and that is not a slip.  jb_ax5b's LISTING pages
! carry no printed page numbers at all -- the "12 11 10 9" down the
! left margin is fanfold carriage-tape line numbering, and the only
! printed numbers are in the front write-up, which is scanned 2-up.
! Every verify_ax5b_*.py here already says "PDF p.NN" for that reason.
!
! WHAT TEST 3A CHECKS.  Reference Manual printed p.50 (PDF p.53):
! "Pseudo-instruction counters may occupy any of the index registers
! as well as main core storage locations but cannot occupy locations
! addressed between 0 and 15."  The test builds a legal pseudo-IC,
! copies it into WORD 9 -- $R, the right half of the accumulator, and
! so an address below 15 -- and issues "EXIC,$R".  Its three error
! messages ARE the contract, and all three are printed on these pages:
!
!   (a) "-NO INTERRUPT WHEN PSEDUO IC / -OF EXIC LESS THAN 15."
!       reached by FALLING THROUGH the EXIC, so the error is that no
!       interruption occurred.  ("PSEDUO" is the listing's own typo;
!       p.108's two messages spell it "PSEUDO".)
!   (b) "-AD NOT SET WHEN PSEUDO IC / -OF EXIC LESS THAN 15."
!       reached from 162103, the handler this test plants in the
!       interrupt entry, when "BADZ,$+1.32" finds AD off.
!   (c) "-INSTRUCT NOT NOPED WHEN PSEUDO / -IC OF EXIC LESS THAN 15."
!       "Z,$X1" zeroes index register 1 before the EXIC, and the
!       subject instruction at 162EXI is "LVI,$X1,%8@777777.40"
!       (024332.00, PDF p.110), which would make it NONZERO.  So
!       "LX,$X1,$X1 / BZXVZ,SERS" -- branch to the error report if the
!       index value is not zero -- is literally "the subject never
!       ran".
!
! THE MANUAL AND THE DECK DISAGREE AT THE BOUNDARY, and this test does
! not settle it: the manual says "between 0 and 15", the deck's three
! messages all say "LESS THAN 15".  The pseudo-IC used here is word 9,
! which is illegal under either reading, so nothing on these pages
! discriminates 15 itself.  Left as the two quotes stand.
!
! THE MACHINERY, row by row.  "SIC,160SX1 / B,160S1" calls routine
! 1260's clear-indicators-0-19 subroutine (022741.00, transcribed in
! programs/ax5b_160s1_clr_inds.strap).  "LVI,$X1,162SUB /
! SVA,$X1,162PSI" aims the pseudo-IC word at the subject slot;
! "LX,$X1,162EXI / SX,$X1,162SUB" loads the subject instruction into
! that slot; "LX,$X1,162PSI / SX,$X1,$R" is the whole point -- it
! copies the pseudo-IC into word 9.  "LVI,$X1,162103 / SVA,$X1,162ITE"
! plants the (b)/(c) handler in 162ITE, the common "-ALL INTERRUPTS
! ENTER HERE" landing at 024320.00, and "LVI,$X1,162INT / SV,$X1,$IA"
! points the Interruption Address register at the 64-word table.
!
! ONE ROW IS NOT EXPLAINED BY THESE PAGES.  At 024144.40, between
! "Z,$X1" and "EXIC,$R", stands "%8@DD%BU,32,8@,3740 -ILLEGAL OP." --
! the same 00000003740 word that routine 1260's 160K7 prints at
! 023050.00 under "-ILLEGAL OP, NO. 31." (programs/ax5b_160k_
! constants.strap).  It sits in the straight-line instruction path,
! one half-word before the EXIC, and nothing on pp.107-108 says why an
! operation-code-invalid word belongs there.  It is not a one-off: the
! deck repeats the identical "Z,$X1 / DD / EXIC" triple in TEST 3B at
! 024155.00/024155.40/024156.00.  Stated rather than rationalised, in
! the manner of ax5b_16082_op_ad.strap's "NOT TRACED" block; the
! ENCODING of the row is settled either way, and that is what this
! file checks.
!
! SINCE THIS FILE WAS WRITTEN, TEST 1CC (pp.93-94) SETTLED WHAT THE
! WORD IS: an enable-state probe.  An operation-code-invalid word
! actuates OP, indicator 15, and mask bits 0-19 are permanently one, so
! executing one interrupts iff the interruption system is enabled --
! and 1CC uses it twice in opposite polarities with error text that
! pins both directions.  It did NOT settle what the word is doing
! HERE; ax5b_162_test3b.strap works through why the probe reading and
! this block's required control flow contradict each other, and names
! the two untranscribed pages that would decide it.  Read that note
! before treating the row as explained.
!
! NOTHING HERE IS A FIRST for this assembler, and saying so is the
! point.  EXIC is already witnessed by TEST 2B (programs/ax5b_162_
! exic_classes.strap), BADZ's trailing-Z clear bit by 16086B and
! SIP17, BZXVZ by TEST 2B, "$+1.32" by ibox3_sva_full's BXE rows, $IA
! by 16086.  What TEST 3A adds is a SECOND, independent listing
! witness for EXIC -- this one with a SYSTEM SYMBOL operand, "EXIC,$R"
! at 024145.00, where 2B only ever wrote "EXIC,162PSI" -- plus 23 more
! rows of field placement and the pseudo-IC legality rule itself.
!
! AND IT UPGRADES TEST 2B'S WEAKEST CLAIM.  ax5b_162_exic_classes.
! strap's header says of 162ITE/162PSI/162SUB: "No label row defining
! any 162* symbol appears on PDF p.101; each address comes from an
! OPERAND field."  PDF p.109 defines them in its own LABEL column,
! read here at 600 dpi:
!     162INT  DR%BU,64,8@,64  -INTRPT TABLE.          024220.00
!     162ITE  BD,$   -ALL INTERRUPTS ENTER HERE.      024320.00
!     162PSI  LX,$X0,0        -PSEUDO IC.             024323.00
!     162SUB  XW,0,0,0        -SUBJ INST.             024324.00
! and PDF p.110 defines 162EXI at 024332.00.  Every one agrees with
! the operand fields on pp.107-108.
!
! ENCODING ONLY, and it could not be otherwise: a run needs the 64-word
! interrupt table, SSIP's SEN/SERS reporting, 160S1's body, and an
! EXIC the model actually EXECUTES.  EXIC is in MISC_CODES, so the
! ASSEMBLER encodes it; that is the whole distinction.
!
! Transcription standard: bit-exact against the printed machine code,
! verify_ax5b_162_test3a_listing.py.
!
! SUBSTITUTIONS: two.  Numeric labels prefixed "L" (L162100, L162103),
! as ax5b_162_exic_classes.strap already does for 1262.  And the DD's
! datum, printed "%8@DD%BU,32,8@,3740", is written "(8)3740" -- the
! same spelling ax5b_160k_constants.strap uses for the identical word,
! which carries no reason there.  The reason, measured rather than
! assumed: assembling this block with the operand as a bare "3740"
! produces 00000007234, because this assembler's default radix is
! DECIMAL (3740 = 0o7234) and the listing's is octal.  The "(8)" is
! load-bearing, not decoration.
!
! EXTERNALS, SYN'd at the addresses this same listing prints.  THESE
! ARE INPUTS TO THE CHECK, NOT WITNESSES -- the same caveat
! verify_ax5b_16082_16083_listing.py makes about L16088.  A SYN row
! MAKES the address field come out right, so the rows naming one prove
! only that every OTHER field lands where the listing puts it.  The
! block has exactly TWO genuine address witnesses: L162103, whose
! address depends on all seventeen preceding half-words being sized
! right, and the self-relative "$+1.32" at 024146.40.  L162100 is NOT
! a third -- the SLC above sets the counter to 024136.0 and L162100 is
! the first label after it, so checking it checks the SLC against the
! number this transcription fed the SLC.  It is asserted anyway, as
! the block's anchor, but it is not evidence.

L160SX1 SYN, (8)23041.0            ! 1260's SIC return link (also p.41)
L160S1  SYN, (8)22741.0            ! 1260's "CLR INDS 0-19" subroutine
SEN     SYN, (8)1310.0             ! the SIC error-entry link
SERS    SYN, (8)1304.0             ! the error-report routine
L162INT SYN, (8)24220.0            ! the 64-word interrupt table, PDF p.109
L162ITE SYN, (8)24320.0            ! "-ALL INTERRUPTS ENTER HERE", p.109
L162PSI SYN, (8)24323.0            ! the pseudo-IC word, p.109
L162SUB SYN, (8)24324.0            ! the subject-instruction slot, p.109
L162EXI SYN, (8)24332.0            ! the IMMED IX subject, PDF p.110
        SLC, (8)24136.0
!
! ---- set the trap up, then put the pseudo-IC where it is illegal ----
L162100 SIC, L160SX1               ! -TEST 3A, PSEUDO IC LESS THAN 15.
        B,   L160S1                !   clear indicators 0-19
        LVI, $X1, L162SUB
        SVA, $X1, L162PSI          ! aim the pseudo-IC at the subject slot
        LX,  $X1, L162EXI          ! the IMMED IX subject instruction
        SX,  $X1, L162SUB
        LX,  $X1, L162PSI
        SX,  $X1, $R               ! THE TEST: pseudo-IC into word 9
        LVI, $X1, L162103
        SVA, $X1, L162ITE          ! plant the handler in the entry
        LVI, $X1, L162INT
        SV,  $X1, $IA              ! point $IA at the 64-word table
        Z,   $X1                   ! so a subject that ran shows up
        DD(BU,32,8), (8)3740       ! -ILLEGAL OP.  (see header)
        EXIC, $R
        SIC, SEN                   ! -NO INTERRUPT WHEN PSEDUO IC
        BD,  SERS                  ! -OF EXIC LESS THAN 15.
!
! ---- 162103: where the interruption lands; rules (b) and (c) -------
L162103 BADZ, $+1.32               ! AD on -> skip the error, clearing it
        SIC, SEN                   ! -AD NOT SET WHEN PSEUDO IC
        BD,  SERS                  ! -OF EXIC LESS THAN 15.
        LX,  $X1, $X1
        SIC, SEN                   ! -INSTRUCT NOT NOPED WHEN PSEUDO
        BZXVZ, SERS                ! -IC OF EXIC LESS THAN 15.
        END, L162100
